From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ashhart <71890694+ashhart@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:39:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/33] Stage remaining synchronous CUDA readbacks on
 integrated GPUs

Upstream TensorFold commit by ashhart, ported onto this series (upstream main e9ee73834161).

Refs #2102.

Route unowned spans through DeviceBuffer.download so integrated devices use
its pinned bounce and discrete devices retain their direct copy. Preserve
each caller's source, destination and byte count, including developer checks.

Release the current thread's bounce and device reading before its driver
closes. Exercise every changed copy expression on both fake device classes,
plus chunk offsets, tails and driver lifetime.

(cherry picked from commit e9ee73834)

Adapted in this series: the readback-site sweep (zig/build/cuda_readback_host.zig, cuda_readback_sites.zig,
zig/tests/cuda/staged_copy_fake.zig) embeds upstream files this fork does not carry, so it is left out;
test-staged-copies-host runs the staging lifetime tests instead. Our own raw synchronous readbacks on the
Flash Next path go through cuda.memory.download too: the window and mixed-round host logits, the lone
head logits row, the MTP ops idle copy and the routing-count capture.
